# Line-ending policy.
#
# Git on Windows commonly runs with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to
# CRLF on checkout. That is harmless for Python sources, but fatal for files a
# Linux container *executes*: `docker build` copies the working tree, so a
# CRLF shebang lands in the image and the container dies at startup with
#
#     env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory        (exit 127)
#
# Pin LF for shell scripts so a Windows clone still produces a working image.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Copied into the image and used at build/run time; keep them LF for the same
# reason (line continuations and shebangs must not carry CRs).
Dockerfile text eol=lf
infra/entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
